Caveats: the paper trains on 10 classes at 713×713 and reports the full 448-image test; we train a 5-channel task (other classes decoded as "other") at 768×576 with 50 labels (3.5 % of 1,445). The 5-class decode removes confusions with tree/grass/vehicle/pool, which can inflate our IoU a little. eval100 is a stratified subset (50 % with flooded road/building), not the paper split.

Near-duplicates (src/dupes.py): test photos showing the same ground as a support photo: {'20shot': 9, '50shot': 14} of 448; without them: {'floodnet/50/floodnet_test_eval100/tau0.5': 0.356, 'floodnet/50/floodnet_test_eval100/tuned': 0.523, 'floodnet/50/floodnet_test_full/tau0.5': 0.279, 'floodnet/50/floodnet_test_full/tuned': 0.509}

Test-time flips (4 views, src/tta.py, on the published model): not adopted. Rule fixed before looking at test: adopt TTA if its val30-tuned mIoU beats the plain one on val30 and the paired full-test difference with each run's own decode is clearly positive. val30 +0.015 [-0.006, +0.032], full test -0.017 [-0.027, -0.007]. **Not adopted: the headline stays the plain model.** Cost: 4x inference (about 70 s instead of 17 s per photo on a T4).
